sequenceDiagram
    title ZDAD-34: Overview Dashboard API

    participant User
    participant Route as Route<br/>(src/routes/overview_route.py)
    participant Service as Service<br/>(src/services/overview_service.py)
    participant Repository as Repository<br/>(src/repositories/)
    participant Database
    participant Jira

    %% Overview Endpoint
    User->>Route: GET /api/v1/overview?period=last_week&specialization=devsecops
    Route->>Route: Decrypt token using private key
    Route->>Jira: Validate Jira email from token
    Jira-->>Route: User exists and is active
    Route->>Service: Get overview metrics (period, specialization)
    Service->>Service: Validate query params (period, specialization)
    Service->>Repository: Fetch kpi_history by specialization and period
    Repository->>Database: SELECT FROM kpi_history<br/>WHERE specialization_id matches<br/>AND within period window
    Database-->>Repository: KPI record (projects_count, completed_count,<br/>active_count, inactive_count, at_risk_count,<br/>not_applicable_count + increase/decrease columns)
    Repository-->>Service: KPI data
    Service->>Service: Determine trend per tile:<br/>increase_count > 0 → "increase"<br/>decrease_count > 0 → "decrease"<br/>both 0 → "flat"
    Service-->>Route: {metrics, statusDistribution, attentionBanner}
    Route-->>User: 200 OK

    %% Filters Endpoint
    User->>Route: GET /api/v1/filters
    Route->>Route: Decrypt token + validate Jira email
    Route->>Service: Get all filter options
    Service->>Repository: Fetch specializations
    Repository->>Database: SELECT specialization_id, specialization_name<br/>FROM specializations WHERE is_active = 1
    Database-->>Repository: Specializations list
    Repository-->>Service: Specializations
    Service->>Repository: Fetch clients
    Repository->>Database: SELECT DISTINCT client<br/>FROM projects WHERE is_active = 1
    Database-->>Repository: Clients list
    Repository-->>Service: Clients
    Service->>Repository: Fetch statuses
    Repository->>Database: SELECT status_id, status_name<br/>FROM statuses WHERE is_active = 1
    Database-->>Repository: Statuses list
    Repository-->>Service: Statuses
    Service-->>Route: {specializations, clients, statuses}
    Route-->>User: 200 OK

    %% Error Scenario
    Note over Route,Database: On unhandled exception
    Service->>Repository: Log error
    Repository->>Database: INSERT INTO error_log<br/>(error_message, error_function, stack_trace)
    Route-->>User: 500 - An unexpected error occurred
